{"parentUuid":"6944995c-dc0b-4ed9-bd8c-fb86bef6f882","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"ae3590b7e2f938057","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JQCkLCVacGTWfPSwuP9Pvz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CaDiCaL 2.0 implementation paper data structure CAV 2024 Biere\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL 2.0 CAV'24 Tool-Paper Artifact\",\"url\":\"https://zenodo.org/records/10943125\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - arminbiere/cadical: CaDiCaL SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical\"},{\"title\":\"dblp: CaDiCaL 2.0.\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/rec/conf/cav/BiereFFFFP24.html\"},{\"title\":\"Available CAV Evaluation Artifact Reusable CAV Evaluation Artifact CaDiCaL 2.0\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFazekasFleuryFroleyksPollitt-CAV24.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL 2.0 Armin Biere1,2(B) , Tobias Faller1 , Katalin Fazekas3\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFazekasFleuryFroleyksPollitt-CAV24-Springer.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Accepted Papers | CAV 2024\",\"url\":\"https://i-cav.org/2024/accepted-papers/\"},{\"title\":\"cadical/README.md at master · arminbiere/cadical\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/arminbiere/cadical/blob/master/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] CaDiCaL 2.0 | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/CaDiCaL-2.0-Biere-Faller/c0e4581f9af5680b764797c6e5e57ca0c6c3078e\"},{\"title\":\"CaDiCaL 2.0 | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-65627-9_7\"},{\"title\":\"Revisiting DRUP-Based Interpolants with CaDiCaL 2.0 | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-90653-4_5\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the CaDiCaL 2.0 implementation paper presented at CAV 2024. Here are the key details:\n\n## Publication Details\n\nThe CaDiCaL 2.0 paper by Armin Biere, Tobias Faller, Katalin Fazekas, Mathias Fleury, Nils Froleyks and Florian Pollitt was published in the Proceedings of Computer Aided Verification - 26th International Conference (CAV'24) in Lecture Notes in Computer Science (LNCS) vol. 14681, pages 133-152, Springer 2024.\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\nCaDiCaL is a modern SAT solver with many features written in C++. It can be used as a stand-alone application through the command-line interface (CLI) or as library through its application programming interface (API) in C++ (or in limited form in C).\n\nRegarding the data structures, the central component, called Internal, implements CDCL search and formula simplification techniques. On top of it, the External facade hides the internals while maintaining the proofs and solutions (aka models) of solved problems.\n\n## Paper Content\n\nIn this tool paper the authors give a high-level introduction into the solver architecture and then go briefly over implemented techniques. They describe basic features and novel advanced usage scenarios.\n\nExperiments confirm that CaDiCaL despite this flexibility has state-of-the-art performance both in a stand-alone as well as incremental setting.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5c9d06f2-4d6a-4e44-a060-40a82ddaebfe","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:13.609Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6944995c-dc0b-4ed9-bd8c-fb86bef6f882","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
