{"parentUuid":"5ca7ca2b-e596-4d15-b31b-f02959a0c95b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"ae3590b7e2f938057","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013UjU9CCNh1MYWieJwEJ7yE","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT 9.10 9.11 release notes performance memory layout watch literal\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Release Notes | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/support/release_notes\"},{\"title\":\"memory layout | Wonderings of a SAT geek\",\"url\":\"https://www.msoos.org/tag/memory-layout/\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/releases\"},{\"title\":\"Watched Literals in SAT and CP\",\"url\":\"https://school.a4cp.org/summer2011/slides/Gent/SATCP3.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SAT solver vs. CP solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/Pa5eQUoLnow\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Memory leak on CP SAT solver · Issue #3212 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3212\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: Higher num_search_workers value increases the resolution time · Issue #1921 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1921\"},{\"title\":\"Memory usage while using AddElement constraint\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/enAzF6Cv2vg\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding CP-SAT versions 9.10 and 9.11 and the topics you're interested in:\n\n## Constraint Enforcement Literals\n\nThe CP-SAT solver now checks for constraints that do not support enforcement literals, and the model checker will return an error before solving if such a constraint has an enforcement literal. This appears to be a change in the 9.11 release.\n\n## Version Releases\n\nOR-Tools v9.11 and v9.10 have been released, and CP-SAT solver v9.10.4067 is available.\n\n## Bound Callbacks (version 9.10)\n\nAs of version 9.10, CP-SAT also supports bound callbacks, which are triggered when the proven bound improves.\n\nThe search results from Google's official OR-Tools release notes and documentation provide information about these versions, though the specific details about performance, memory layout, and watched literals in the context of these particular versions aren't comprehensively detailed in the search results. For more detailed release notes on performance improvements and memory layout changes, you may want to consult the official GitHub releases page for OR-Tools directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5969d613-4008-424f-aae0-557dd0a38150","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:25.856Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5ca7ca2b-e596-4d15-b31b-f02959a0c95b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f0c72463-ce27-4444-8554-3d2babe295a9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"ae3590b7e2f938057","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fp9D8rYTEJN8g8D5bApmAJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP solver Gecode Choco propagator cache memory locality 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Making Compact-Table Compact | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-98334-9_14\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - chuffed/chuffed: The Chuffed CP solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/chuffed/chuffed\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · chocoteam/choco-solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/chocoteam/choco-solver/releases\"},{\"title\":\"Choco Solver Documentation Release 4.0.8\",\"url\":\"https://www.dcs.gla.ac.uk/~pat/cpM/choco4/user_guide-4.0.8.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"A complementary intersection propagator for filtering the sets. by JLiangWaterloo · Pull Request #449 · chocoteam/choco-solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/chocoteam/choco-solver/pull/449\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Choco-solver: A Java library for constraint programming\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/364511270_Choco-solver_A_Java_library_for_constraint_programming\"},{\"title\":\"The CHOCO constraint programming solver | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/230668970_The_CHOCO_constraint_programming_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Choco-solver\",\"url\":\"https://choco-solver.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Propagator (org.choco-solver-choco-solver 4.0.2 API)\",\"url\":\"https://javadoc.io/static/org.choco-solver/choco-solver/4.0.2/org/chocosolver/solver/constraints/Propagator.html\"},{\"title\":\"custom propagator needed ? · google/or-tools · Discussion #3303\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3303\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found relevant information about constraint programming solvers (Gecode and Choco) and propagators, though the results don't specifically focus on cache memory locality research from 2024. Here's what I found:\n\n## Key Information on CP Solvers and Propagators\n\nResearch on propagators in Gecode has included cache analysis, with compact-table techniques achieving almost an order of magnitude faster runtime while using half the memory compared to Gecode's original implementations.\n\nOptimization techniques for propagators include making sparse bit-sets dynamically compact so that only their essential parts occupy memory, with their implementation dynamically adapted during search.\n\nRegarding the Choco solver, Choco is an open-source Java library dedicated to Constraint Programming. A propagator removes, from the domains of the target variables, values that cannot correspond to a valid combination of values.\n\nThe search results provide information about propagator design and optimization in constraint solvers, but they do not contain specific 2024 research papers or articles specifically focused on cache memory locality optimization in the context of CP solvers like Gecode and Choco. If you're looking for very recent 2024-specific research on this topic, you may need to check academic databases like arXiv, DBLP, or conference proceedings from CP conferences held in 2024.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c43144fd-c137-4035-b304-443d74c0aa37","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:27.913Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f0c72463-ce27-4444-8554-3d2babe295a9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"51b58b5a-da04-40aa-87d3-ee610f1f7785","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"ae3590b7e2f938057","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016BFDokdLArbstRUeymuZzS","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"sat_inprocessing\" OR \"linear_propagator\" OR \"integer_trail\" OR-Tools cache memory benchmark\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SAT Solving with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7979176/\"},{\"title\":\"dblp: Memory Efficient Parallel SAT Solving with Inprocessing.\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/rec/conf/ictai/IserBS19.html\"},{\"title\":\"Certified SAT solving with GPU accelerated inprocessing\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/OsamaWijsBiere-FMSD23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solving with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing\",\"url\":\"https://gears.win.tue.nl/papers/parafrost_gpu.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Cache Performance of SAT Solvers: a Case Study for Efficient Implementation of Algorithms | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-540-24605-3_22\"},{\"title\":\"Certified SAT solving with GPU accelerated inprocessing | Formal Methods in System Design | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10703-023-00432-z\"},{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 81 (2024) 989-1017\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solving with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing Muhammad Osama (\\u0000)1 ∗\",\"url\":\"https://d-nb.info/1304678997/34\"},{\"title\":\"SatPropagator | OR-Tools | Google Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/sat/sat_base/SatPropagator\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solving with GPU Accelerated Inprocessing | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-72016-2_8\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found regarding your query about SAT inprocessing, linear propagators, integer trails, and OR-Tools cache memory benchmarking:\n\n## SAT Inprocessing\n\nSince 2013, the leading SAT solvers in the SAT competition all use inprocessing, which unlike preprocessing, interleaves search with simplifications. However, applying inprocessing frequently can still be a bottle neck, i.e., for hard or large formulas.\n\nResearchers have introduced the first attempt to parallelize inprocessing on GPU architectures, presenting new space-efficient data structures and devising a data-parallel garbage collector.\n\n## Memory and Cache Performance\n\nCache performance of different SAT solvers has been experimentally evaluated as a case study for efficient implementation of SAT algorithms, examining several different Boolean Constraint Propagation (BCP) mechanisms and their respective run time and cache performances on selected benchmark instances. A cache friendly data structure is a key element in the efficient implementation of SAT solvers.\n\n## Data Structures for SAT Solving\n\nTo efficiently implement inprocessing techniques for GPU architectures, researchers designed new data structures from scratch to count the number of learnt clauses, and store other relevant clause information, while keeping the memory consumption as low as possible.\n\nThe search results primarily cover GPU-accelerated SAT inprocessing research, but don't contain specific information about \"linear_propagator\" or \"integer_trail\" as distinct OR-Tools components, nor do they include benchmarks specifically comparing OR-Tools cache memory usage.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"adf87f4e-008e-42ec-b97a-cf7cd81d031d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:28.702Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"51b58b5a-da04-40aa-87d3-ee610f1f7785","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_