{"parentUuid":"2e25dd92-951d-4af3-a1e5-989c49f1130e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ae3590b7e2f938057","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01V5f2HapFKkCwb7rP2TggqT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WvFQqmNnQHN6oJwKvrg3ZX","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"CP-SAT parameter \"linearization_level\" \"boolean_encoding_level\" worker tuning long running"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6990,"cache_read_input_tokens":41038,"output_tokens":222,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6990},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":222,"cache_read_input_tokens":41038,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6990,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6990,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caozg6SqjCZJaguhCXRUt","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c9460bae-82df-4aee-9962-bd5a5b5f1c0f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:50.213Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c9460bae-82df-4aee-9962-bd5a5b5f1c0f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"ae3590b7e2f938057","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WvFQqmNnQHN6oJwKvrg3ZX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT parameter \"linearization_level\" \"boolean_encoding_level\" worker tuning long running\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Selecting SAT Encodings for Pseudo-Boolean and Linear Integer Constraints\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol235-cp2022/LIPIcs.CP.2022.38/LIPIcs.CP.2022.38.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy.solvers.ortools — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/extra-require/_modules/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"Learning to select SAT encodings for pseudo-Boolean and linear integer constraints | Constraints | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10601-023-09364-1\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT for scheduling Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://schedulingseminar.com/presentations/SchedulingSeminar_LaurentPerron.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"A Compact Encoding of Pseudo-Boolean Constraints into SAT | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-33347-7_10\"}]\n\nI found relevant information about CP-SAT parameters related to your search. Here are the key findings:\n\n## CP-SAT Parameters\n\nThe `linearization_level` parameter can be set to 0 to disable linearisation (default: 1, can also set to 2), and `boolean_encoding_level` has a default value of 1.\n\nExample tuning parameters for long-running problems include `num_search_workers=8` for parallel workers (default: 8), `log_search_progress=True` to log the search process, and `cp_model_presolve=False` to disable presolve (default: True, almost always beneficial).\n\n## How These Parameters Work\n\nThe parameters relate to how CP-SAT encodes constraints:\n\nCP-SAT works by converting all integer variables into boolean variables. For each potential value, it creates two boolean variables: one indicating whether the integer variable is equal to this value, and another indicating whether it is less than or equal to it. This is called an order encoding.\n\nDefault parameters include `optimize_with_core': False`, `search_branching': 0`, `core_minimization_level': 2`, `cp_model_probing_level': 2`, `cp_model_presolve': True`, `use_phase_saving': True`.\n\nFor long-running problems, adjusting the linearization level and boolean encoding level, combined with worker tuning, can significantly impact solver performance.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"12e693b8-9282-4e46-9ba4-f2ff978328e0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:56.777Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c9460bae-82df-4aee-9962-bd5a5b5f1c0f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2e25dd92-951d-4af3-a1e5-989c49f1130e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"ae3590b7e2f938057","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KRrgPXa9XMjEfY7JUA3erz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Cache Performance of SAT Solvers\" Hoelldobler Manthey case study BCP implementation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Cache Performance of SAT Solvers: a Case Study for Efficient Implementation of Algorithms | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-540-24605-3_22\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Improving Resource-Unaware SAT Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220896083_Improving_Resource-Unaware_SAT_Solvers\"},{\"title\":\"Improving Resource-Unaware SAT Solvers | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-16242-8_37\"},{\"title\":\"Cache performance of SAT solvers: A case study for efficient implementation of algorithms - Princeton University\",\"url\":\"https://collaborate.princeton.edu/en/publications/cache-performance-of-sat-solvers-a-case-study-for-efficient-imple\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Improving resource-unaware sat solvers\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/1013536/Improving_resource_unaware_sat_solvers\"},{\"title\":\"Cache Performance of SAT Solvers: A Case Study for Eﬃcient Implementation of\",\"url\":\"https://www.ccs.neu.edu/home/lieber/courses/csg260/f06/materials/papers/sat/SAT_2003_cache.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Cache Performance of SAT Solvers: a Case Study for Efficient Implementation of Algorithms | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220944485_Cache_Performance_of_SAT_Solvers_a_Case_Study_for_Efficient_Implementation_of_Algorithms\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] Improving Resource-Unaware SAT Solvers | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Improving-Resource-Unaware-SAT-Solvers-H%C3%B6lldobler-Manthey/7655dc29b40ecba69893136a36320df863d92cd2\"},{\"title\":\"Towards Improving the Resource Usage of SAT solvers Norbert Manthey∗\",\"url\":\"https://easychair.org/publications/download/9W\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A Lightweight Component Caching Scheme for Satisfiability Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220944633_A_Lightweight_Component_Caching_Scheme_for_Satisfiability_Solvers\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about cache performance of SAT solvers, though I should clarify that the main \"Cache Performance of SAT Solvers\" case study appears to be by Zhang and Malik (2004), not Hölldobler and Manthey. However, Hölldobler and Manthey did conduct related work on this topic.\n\n## Main Case Study: Cache Performance of SAT Solvers\n\nThe seminal case study experimentally evaluates the cache performance of different SAT solvers and evaluates several different Boolean Constraint Propagation (BCP) mechanisms, showing their respective run time and cache performances on selected benchmark instances.\n\n### Key Findings:\n\nA cache friendly data structure is a key element in the efficient implementation of SAT solvers. The study shows empirical cache miss rates of several modern SAT solvers based on the Davis-Logemann-Loveland (DLL) algorithm with learning and non-chronological backtracking. Recently developed SAT solvers are much more cache friendly in data structures and algorithm implementations compared with their predecessors.\n\n## Related Work by Hölldobler and Manthey\n\nHölldobler, Manthey and Saptawijaya aimed to show how a resource-unaware SAT solver can be improved by utilizing the cache sensibly. Their work discusses cache utilization in state-of-the-art SAT solvers, with the aim to show how a resource-unaware SAT solver can be improved by utilizing the cache sensibly, performing the analysis on a CDCL-based SAT solver using a subset of the industrial SAT Competition 2009 benchmark. Several techniques resulted in a combined speedup up to 83% without affecting the search path of the solver.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6fb63d04-5d21-42c5-871d-54e681197e9a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:58.858Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2e25dd92-951d-4af3-a1e5-989c49f1130e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6fb63d04-5d21-42c5-871d-54e681197e9a","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ae3590b7e2f938057","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011BtxFfq3ozskVp5KF43x5y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have sufficient material. Let me synthesize the findings into a focused research summary.\n\n---\n\n# Cache-aware/Cache-oblivious 数据结构在 CP/SAT solver 内核的应用调研\n\n**目标硬件：** i9-13900KS（L1=80KB/core, L2=2MB/core, L3=36MB shared），CP-SAT long-running 求解。\n\n## 1. CDCL solver 的 cache profile（基线事实）\n\n经典结论（Zhang & Malik 2003 SAT 论文 + Chaff 实现报告）：\n- **L2 miss penalty 100-200 cycles**，CDCL 求解 **60-70% runtime 是在等内存**\n- 两文字 watch（two-watched literals）的 cache 收益是关键：watch list 中存 literal 本身，**50-90% 的情况不用真去摸 clause 内存**\n- watchlist 的 spatial locality 远好于\"散落在 heap 里的 clause\"\n\nHölldobler / Manthey / Saptawijaya 的 follow-up（CDCL 解算器上）：纯做 cache-aware 改造，**不改搜索路径，组合速度提升最高 83%**。关键技术：blocking literal 内嵌、binary/ternary clause specialization、按 cache line 紧凑打包 clause metadata。\n\n## 2. SoA vs AoS 在 watch list 的实证\n\n工业经验（Mate Soos / msoos.org，CryptoMiniSat 作者）：\n- 真实痛点不是 SoA vs AoS 的整片切换，而是 **clause arena 的连续内存分配**（自定义 memory manager）。Soos 花 3 天调试 CryptoMiniSat 比 MiniSat 慢，根因是 allocator 的分配位置导致 cache 失效\n- **lingeling 的 binary clause 隐式存储**：watch list 元素首位 tag 区分长/短 clause，**80% clause 是 binary 的场景下省 ~50% 空间**\n- Algorithmica HPC 教材 / Intel Memory Layout Transformations：SoA 在\"只读一个字段 / 可向量化\"路径下提速 40-60%；watch list 的 propagation 路径是典型\"只读 watcher 元数据再决定要不要摸 clause\"，理论吻合 SoA 收益场景\n\n## 3. Bit-parallel data structures（roaring / sparse bitset）\n\n- **Compact-Table（CT）算法**：Demeulenaere et al. 2016，用 reversible sparse bit-set 做 table constraint GAC。**已是 OR-Tools 和 OscaR 的默认 table propagator**。\"Making Compact-Table Compact\"（CP 2018）进一步把 sparse bitset 做成\"运行时按需 compact\"，比原 Gecode 实现 **快近一个数量级、内存减半**\n- **Roaring bitmap**：在 SAT/CP 内核里没看到主流采用的实证论文（2024-2026 没找到），主要原因是 watch list 的稀疏度模式（每个 var 只有几个 watcher）不在 roaring 的最佳工作区\n- bit-parallel 的真正胜利点是 **table constraint 和 reified clause group**，不是 watch list\n\n## 4. Cache-conscious clause storage\n\n- Stuckey/Sulzmann 在 JSAT 2009《Cache Conscious Data Structures for Boolean Satisfiability Solvers》把 MiniSat 2.0 改造，blocking literal 嵌入 watch entry、按 cache line 对齐 clause header，**15-20% 提速**\n- **CaDiCaL 2.0（CAV 2024，Biere et al.）** 没在论文里大书特书 cache 改造，但代码层面延续了 binary clause 内嵌 watch、64-byte 对齐的传统\n- **Kissat（SAT Competition 2024 三金）** 用 C 重写就是为了\"对内存布局 full control\"，比 CaDiCaL 内存更紧、单实例更快\n\n## 5. CP-SAT 内部数据布局（公开材料）\n\nPerron / Didier 在 CP 2023 *The CP-SAT-LP Solver* 论文里提到：\n- **literal 仍用 32 位**（明确说扩到 64 位会\"negatively impact memory consumption and cache usage\"）\n- propagator 用 **优先级队列**（LP relaxation 优先级最低）\n- LP 约束分小批量加入 cut pool（也是 cache 敏感的设计）\n\n但 OR-Tools 团队**没有公开过任何 cache-miss profiling 数据或 SoA/AoS 切换实验**。release notes 9.10/9.11/9.12 都没把\"cache layout\"作为单独 changelog 项目——很可能是渐进微调，没大刀阔斧改。\n\n## 6. 与 Round 6 #aa2c（march+LTO+PGO）的协同\n\nawesome-pgo（zamazan4ik 维护）汇总的真实生产数据：\n- LTO 单做 +3-7%，PGO 单做 +5-10%（C++ 整数密集），LTO+PGO 叠加在热循环里能到 +20-30%\n- **PGO 的杀手特性是 layout：guided basic-block reordering + function ordering，正好是 cache-line / I-cache 收益**\n- Ayupov 2024 的 BOLT/AutoFDO 改进让 LBR 采样能拿到全 instrumentation 93% 的收益、overhead < 2%——意思是 long-running 的 168h 模式很适合直接采样而不是侵入式插桩\n- 没有专门\"SAT solver + PGO\"的论文，但 Factorio、resvg 等同量级 C++ 应用 PGO 实测都在 +10% 量级，**和 cache 改造可以叠加**\n\n## 7. Profile-guided 数据布局（PGO data layout）\n\n- PGO 主流仍是 code layout（hot/cold split, BB reorder）\n- **数据布局 PGO**（heap object reordering）：Google AutoFDO + LLVM Propeller 在大规模搜索引擎实测有效，但**编译器原生支持还不成熟**，CP/SAT 领域没有公开成果\n- 实际可做的是手工 SoA + cacheline pad，PGO 本身不会自动重排数据\n\n---\n\n## 对 CP-SAT 用户层（不改 OR-Tools 源码）能做的\n\n1. **THP（透明大页）打开 + tcmalloc/jemalloc 替换默认 malloc**。168h 长跑的 working set 可能十几 GB，TLB miss 削减是免费收益。Windows 等价是 Large Pages 权限 + mimalloc。**预计 1-5%**（无需任何改代码）\n2. **march=native + LTO + PGO 三件套**。168h 模式正适合先跑 8-24h instrumented build 采 profile，然后用 profile 重编 OR-Tools wheel。**预计 10-20%**，是不改逻辑能拿到的最大单项\n3. **进程级 NUMA / CPU pinning + L3 隔离**。13900KS 是单 socket 但有 P/E core 异构，把 CP-SAT worker 钉在 P-core、避免 E-core 抢 L3 - 这是用户层 affinity 设置，不动 OR-Tools\n4. **worker matrix 减少冷启动**：每个 worker profile 独立调 `linearization_level` / `boolean_encoding_level` / `cp_model_probing_level`，让热数据稳定在 L2（2MB/core），不要让 LP 松弛把 cache 全冲走\n5. **同时跑多 base / 多候选时控制并发数**：4 worker × 大 base 比 8 worker × 大 base cache 命中好得多（L3 36MB 是固定预算）\n6. **不要做的**：自己写 propagator 嵌进 CP-SAT、改 watch list ABI、把 literal 扩到 64 位 - 都是 Perron 文档明确警告的 cache 杀手\n7. **AI sidecar 路径（项目 Phase 3B C 道）**：用 AI 提示 candidate ordering 时，**让 hot candidate 在前面**，让 master model 的常用子集稳定在 L2，是合规且与 cache 协同的玩法\n\n**预期总收益：仅靠用户层（含 PGO）叠加，long-running 工作负载有望拿到 15-30%。**这是\"几百个百分比\"的零头——要拿到几百个百分比，必须改 OR-Tools 内核或换 solver，但那破坏 PROJECT_LOCK 的\"certified path\"，不是当前阶段该做的事。\n\n---\n\nSources:\n- [Cache Performance of SAT Solvers (Zhang & Malik, SAT 2003)](https://www.ccs.neu.edu/home/lieber/courses/csg260/f06/materials/papers/sat/SAT_2003_cache.pdf)\n- [Improving Resource-Unaware SAT Solvers (Hölldobler, Manthey, Saptawijaya)](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-16242-8_37)\n- [Cache Conscious Data Structures for SAT (Stuckey et al., JSAT 2009)](https://people.eng.unimelb.edu.au/pstuckey/papers/jsat09.pdf)\n- [Mate Soos memory layout posts](https://www.msoos.org/tag/memory-layout/)\n- [CaDiCaL 2.0 (Biere et al., CAV 2024)](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-65627-9_7)\n- [CaDiCaL/Kissat SAT Competition 2024 description](https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/BiereFallerFazekasFleuryFroleyksPollitt-SAT-Competition-2024-solvers.pdf)\n- [Kissat SAT solver](https://github.com/arminbiere/kissat)\n- [The CP-SAT-LP Solver (Perron, Didier, Gay - CP 2023)](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol280-cp2023/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3.pdf)\n- [CP-SAT Primer (under the hood)](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html)\n- [Compact-Table: Reversible Sparse Bit-Sets (CP 2016)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1604.06641)\n- [Making Compact-Table Compact (CP 2018)](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-98334-9_14)\n- [SoA vs AoS - Algorithmica HPC](https://en.algorithmica.org/hpc/cpu-cache/aos-soa/)\n- [Intel Memory Layout Transformations](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/articles/technical/memory-layout-transformations.html)\n- [awesome-pgo - PGO real-world results](https://github.com/zamazan4ik/awesome-pgo)\n- [From Profiling to Optimization: PGO survey (Ayupov et al., 2024)](https://arxiv.org/html/2507.16649v1)\n- [Transparent Hugepages performance impact](https://alexandrnikitin.github.io/blog/transparent-hugepages-measuring-the-performance-impact/)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1378,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1762,"cache_read_input_tokens":48028,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1762,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaozhGwPtfbfxQZQFLRCi","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"9d81f4a8-424b-4e41-abe6-26abda5a4f00","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:28:20.932Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
